<section class="g-dark" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div data-v9-reveal class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">\</span> 01 · How a batch runs</div>
    <h2 data-v9-reveal style="--d:60ms">Four steps, same bar every time.</h2>
    <p data-v9-reveal class="lead" style="--d:120ms">
      The bar is set once, with your hiring manager. Every candidate after that is held to it, whoever sourced them.
    </p>
    <ol class="cr-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="pf-k">45 minutes, once</span><h3>Set the bar</h3><p>
          An intake call with your hiring manager. The skills that matter, weighted, written down and agreed.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="pf-k">Any source</span><h3>Send the candidates</h3><p>
          From your recruiters, agencies, referrals or careers page. Three or thirty.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="pf-k">30 to 45 minutes each</span><h3>We interview them</h3><p>
          Questions written from each candidate’s own CV, by someone who has done the job. Recorded with consent.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="pf-k">About 48 hours</span><h3>You get the ranking</h3><p>
          Every score with its evidence, the open questions named, and which sources sent people who cleared the bar.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
